  >   storage  volume problems  see key 9 STORAGE: its findings carry their own next commands

  >   restart  crash loop  what usually fixes it
      note   the previous logs (above) show the exit reason; a config or Secret change is the usual cause - compare with the last rollout:
      read   kubectl --context kdash-local -n kdash-e2e rollout history deployment/DEPLOYMENT  # what changed and when

  >   scheduling  pods not placed  what usually fixes it
      read   kubectl --context kdash-local describe nodes | grep -A 8 'Allocated resources'  # free capacity per node
      note   reduce requests, add capacity, or fix the nodeSelector / affinity / taint tolerations the scheduler message names

  >   image  pull failures  what usually fixes it
      read   kubectl --context kdash-local -n kdash-e2e get pods -o jsonpath='{range .items[*]}{.metadata.name}: {.spec.containers[*].image} pullSecrets={.spec.imagePullSecrets[*].name}{"\n"}{end}'  # the image references and pull secrets
      note   check the tag exists in the registry and the pull secret is valid; the registry must be reachable from the nodes

